      "side": 0,
      "message": "Can you clarify this, `It is not intented to use vendor legacy file if the release flag is set to true (or not set for previous)`, the \"not intended\" part is confusing me.\n\nThat to me says that if flag is enabled then:\n```\n#ifdef ENABLE_CAP_AIDL_HYBRID_MODE\n```\nWill be pass (ENABLE_CAP_AIDL_HYBRID_MODE is defined), but it is infact using line 69:\n```\n\"/vendor/etc/parameter-framework/ParameterFrameworkConfigurationPolicy.xml\";\n```\n\nAlso for legacy mode `/vendor/etc/parameter-framework/ParameterFrameworkConfigurationPolicy.xml` should be used. Does this means that `RELEASE_HARDWARE_AUDIO_USE_CAP_AIDL` will be true for legacy devices in AOSP (Android 15)?",
